## Phase 2: User Story 1 - Keyboard Navigation & Mnemonic Overlay Engine (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Enable keyboard-centric navigation, search focus (`Ctrl+Shift+K`), and dynamic 1-2 character mnemonic red-box overlays on UI elements.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T004 [P] [US1] Create hotkey engine plugin in `frontend/plugins/hotkeys.ts` with global listeners.
- [x] T005 [P] [US1] Implement mnemonic generator utility in `frontend/utils/mnemonics.ts` mapping shortcuts to task IDs, tags, projects, and queries.
- [x] T006 [US1] Update `frontend/components/TaskList.vue` to render red-box mnemonic overlay badges over task items.
- [x] T007 [US1] Wire `Ctrl+Shift+K` to focus the search bar across `frontend/pages/index.vue` and `frontend/layouts/default.vue`.

---

## Phase 3: User Story 2 - Active Task Timer & Timewarrior Integration (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Display currently running task widget (`+ACTIVE`), allow starting/stopping timers, and auto-stop previously running tasks.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T008 [P] [US2] Implement active task endpoint (`GET /api/tasks/active`) in `backend/src/tasks.ts`.
- [x] T009 [P] [US2] Implement start and stop timer endpoints (`POST /api/tasks/:uuid/start`, `POST /api/tasks/:uuid/stop`) in `backend/src/tasks.ts`.
- [x] T010 [US2] Extend Vuex state (`frontend/store/index.ts`) with `activeTask` state and timer actions.
- [x] T011 [US2] Create floating timer component `frontend/components/ActiveTaskBar.vue` with start/stop triggers.
- [x] T012 [US2] Integrate `ActiveTaskBar` widget into `frontend/layouts/default.vue`.

---

## Phase 4: User Story 3 - TWKB-Inspired Kanban Board & Gantt Chart Views (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP

**Goal**: Provide a responsive 4-column Kanban board (`To Do`, `In Progress`, `Waiting`, `Done`) and an interactive SVG Gantt Timeline view option.

### Implementation Tasks
- [x] T013 [P] [US3] Create `frontend/components/KanbanCard.vue` displaying urgency, priority chips, project tags, blocked indicators, and inline action buttons.
- [x] T014 [US3] Create `frontend/components/KanbanBoard.vue` implementing 4-column drag-and-drop layout via `vuedraggable`.
- [x] T015 [US3] Wire drag-and-drop state handlers in `KanbanBoard.vue` to trigger timer start (when moved to In Progress) and completion (when moved to Done).
- [x] T016 [US3] Add `Kanban` display mode option to `frontend/pages/index.vue` view switcher.
- [x] T016B [P] [US3B] Create `frontend/components/GanttChart.vue` implementing interactive SVG timeline chart, date span calculation with 1-day fallback, and SVG dependency arrow connectors.
- [x] T016C [US3B] Integrate `Gantt` view mode into `frontend/pages/index.vue` display mode toggle and URL query params (`mode=Gantt`).
- [x] T016D [US3B] Update Gantt dependency arrows to render End-to-Start (right edge of prerequisite to left edge of dependent task positioned below and to the right).
- [x] T016E [US3B] Implement interactive left/right anchor handles on Gantt task bars for drag/click dependency creation and hoverable arrow 'X' delete buttons.
- [x] T016F [US3B] Implement horizontal calendar date sequencing (start -> due -> latest precedent completion -> today fallback; start-to-due inclusive duration).
- [x] T016G [US3B] Implement 4-tier vertical task sorting (Priority H>M>L>none -> Taskwarrior Urgency desc -> Dependents count desc -> Description alphabetical).
- [x] T016H [US3B] Implement real-time "filter as you type" search input in Gantt controls with 2-way debounced URL query synchronization.
- [x] T016I [US3B] Implement multi-track non-overlapping orthogonal dependency arrow routing with semicircular bridge hops and strict intermediate task card obstacle avoidance.
- [x] T016J [US3B] Implement dynamic fluid column width expansion and container width tracking (ResizeObserver) for responsive Week/Month zoom views.
- [x] T016K [US3B] Implement calendarless "Sequence" view mode with numbered step columns (`Step 1`, `Step 2`, ...) starting directly on earliest task day without past buffer.
- [x] T016L [US3B] Eliminate empty weeks/months in timeline ranges, enforce generous column width minimums (700px week, 1500px month) to maintain wide inter-card channels and multi-track routing, and support horizontal scrolling.

